        {
          "type": "text",
          "html": "Hor Drill is a pneumatic drilling unit for horizontal holes the diamond wire passes through. With a pneumatic rotary head and a down-the-hole (DTH) hammer it reaches depths of 25 - 30 metres even in rock with natural irregularities.",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "html": "Light structure that is easy to position for horizontal drilling flush with the block. Column for DTH hammer rods of 1,500 mm and for drill steel of 2,400 mm. The same unit can be fitted with a pneumatic rock drill MA 90 for small-diameter holes with drill steel or conical rods. A down jack with a horizontal pipe lets the column be moved along the drilling line.",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Two versions",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "html": "ID in the model name stands for the hydraulic version.",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Pneumatic (Hor Drill): feed stroke 1,000 - 1,500 mm, rotary torque 850 Nm, air consumption 8 m³/min, weight 230 kg",
            "Hydraulic (Hor Drill ID): feed stroke 1,760 mm, rotary torque 1,600 Nm, rotary speed 35 - 100 rpm, weight 230 kg"
          ],
          "gen": true
        },
